# Localization (DewTime)

All user-facing strings must support Japanese and English.

## Adding new UI text

1. Add a key to `DewTimeLiveActivityShared/L10n.swift` (or `DewTime/Support/L10nModels.swift` / `L10nGarden.swift` for app-only domains)
2. Register **both** `ja` and `en` in `DewTimeLiveActivityShared/Localizable.xcstrings`
3. Use `Text(L10n.Domain.key)` or `L10n.tr("key", default: "日本語")` — never hardcode Japanese in Views/Models/Services/Extensions
4. Use `L10n` for accessibility labels and notification text too

## Logic vs display

- Never compare localized strings (`==`, `switch` on display names, `filter { $0.label == "易しい" }`)
- Use stable enums / IDs: `FishDifficulty`, `DifficultyFilterBand`, product IDs, `Achievement.rawValue`

## Extensions

- `Localizable.xcstrings` must stay in **DewTimeLiveActivityShared** with membership on App + Live Activity Extension targets
- Extension code uses `LocalizationManager.shared` (reads language from App Group `UserDefaults`)

## Glossary

Follow `docs/LOCALIZATION_GLOSSARY.md` for brand terms (しずく → Dew Drop, いってきます → I'm off!, etc.)

## Checklist before finishing

- [ ] xcstrings has ja + en for every new key
- [ ] No hardcoded Japanese in user-facing Swift (except `default:` in L10n and tests)
- [ ] `LocalizationGuardTests` passes
